# The linters whose suppression comments and directives the tree has
# carried since its first commit: `# noqa` codes in `src/` and
# `tests/`, and a `# yamllint disable-line` over the `on:` key in the
# CI workflow. Neither tool ran until the `lint` env in `tox.ini` gave
# them somewhere to run from.
#
# Standalone rather than compiled together with `test.in`: unlike
# `mypy`, none of these resolves the suite's imports, so what they see
# does not depend on what is installed alongside them.
#
# The two below read the CI workflows, which until now no gate opened
# beyond `yamllint` checking that they were well-formed YAML. `zizmor`
# audits them for the ways a workflow leaks a token or runs somebody
# else's code; `check-jsonschema` validates them against GitHub's own
# schema -- catching, locally, the class of typo that otherwise only
# surfaces on a trigger that cannot be fired from a branch.
check-jsonschema
ruff
yamllint
zizmor
